      "EEE",
      "EEEC",
      "ENG"
    ],
    "not_available_to_all_programme_with": [
      "(Admyr 2021-onwards)"
    ],
    "not_available_as_bde_ue_to_programme": [],
    "not_available_as_core_to_programme": [],
    "not_offered_as_unrestricted_elective": false,
    "description": "This course introduces the students to the basic concepts and theory behind techniques and algorithms used in signal processing systems, a topic that forms an integral part of engineering systems in many diverse areas. Emphasis is on different types of signals and systems, and their interrelation and representation using different orthogonal components. Upon completion, the student should be able to understand the fundaments of signals and linear time invariant (LTI) systems, understand and apply Fourier transforms, Laplace transforms, and Z-transform to the analysis and description of signals and LTI systems, and take advanced level courses on the systems area."
  },
