    "not_offered_as_unrestricted_elective": false,
    "description": "Through this course, students should be able to understand the representation of continuous-time and discrete-time signals; their frequency characteristics and Fourier spectrum; representation and characteristics of linear time-invariant systems in both time and frequency domains; and the principles of sampling a continuous-time signal to yield a discrete-time one. Contents: Signals and Systems. Linear Time-Invariant Systems. Fourier Representation of Signals and LTI Systems. Sampling. Modulation."
  },
  {
    "code": "IE3012",
    "title": "COMMUNICATION PRINCIPLES",
    "no_of_credits": "3.0 AU",
    "grading_type": null,
    "prerequisites": [
      "EE2010 OR",
      "IM2004 OR",
      "IE2010 OR",
      "IE2110"
    ],
    "mutually_exclusive": [],
